1
00:00:00,560 --> 00:00:05,000
Where do these
"normal ranges" even come from?

2
00:00:05,000 --> 00:00:10,000
People often picture five professors
in Geneva sipping espresso and declaring:

3
00:00:10,000 --> 00:00:12,900
"Gentlemen, the ideal sperm
must look like Brad Pitt."

4
00:00:12,960 --> 00:00:18,500
Not at all! The WHO gathered results
from thousands of men across five continents.

5
00:00:18,640 --> 00:00:22,700
What did they have in common?
Their partners had all gotten pregnant

6
00:00:22,700 --> 00:00:25,800
in less than a year.

7
00:00:25,920 --> 00:00:28,400
Certified future dads.

8
00:00:28,480 --> 00:00:33,500
Picture a giant class photo:
dads lined up from lowest to highest.

9
00:00:33,600 --> 00:00:38,400
The WHO threshold is just a line drawn
at the very bottom of that photo.

10
00:00:38,560 --> 00:00:40,800
The exact values are
on screen right now.

11
00:00:40,880 --> 00:00:44,000
Guess how many future fathers
are below that line? Zero?

12
00:00:44,000 --> 00:00:47,800
Five out of a hundred!

13
00:00:47,920 --> 00:00:52,400
By definition, 5% of those men
"failed" on paper…

14
00:00:52,480 --> 00:00:55,300
while they were literally assembling
a stroller in the living room!

15
00:00:55,360 --> 00:00:59,000
Why? Because this isn't a
medical school entrance exam—

16
00:00:59,000 --> 00:00:59,950
it's just the front
row of the class photo!
